('127.881.d.7.N',4,'When tinting, a painter should add toner:','["by the cupful", "all at once", "without checking", "in very small amounts and recheck the match"]'::jsonb,3,'Small steps.','original'),
('127.881.d.7.O',3,'The first formula looks off, so Dee checks a variant formula in the database for the same color code. She is:','["identifying an alternative color formula to achieve a blendable match", "quitting", "guessing", "ignoring variants"]'::jsonb,0,'Variants.','original'),
('127.881.d.7.O',4,'A paint code can have several variants because:','["only one plant exists", "factory color varies between plants and batches", "every car is identical", "paint never changes"]'::jsonb,1,'Variants exist.','original')
